From f72f10385c3e6f306e64e42cbc51fe4290bec1ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:38:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Relocate: six house portals, in six towns

A house portal and an estate agent now stand in Rimmington, Taverley,
Pollnivneach, Rellekka, Brimhaven and Yanille. %poh_location says which one
is yours, the estate agent moves it for OSRS's own price, and the other five
tell you where your house actually is.

Relocating changes where the door is and nothing else - the rooms, the
furniture and the style are all in varps of their own and the house is built
into an instance from a template, so there is nothing on the ground to pack
up. The instance is freed before the move so nobody walks out of the old door.

Every tile and facing came back from a pass in game. The tool proposes
footprints that are level, clear, off the road and beside the town's path;
whether a five-tile portal LOOKS right on a slope is not something it can
answer, and getting that wrong cost five shipped placements the first time.

Two things that pass says, that were written down wrong before:

- Rotation is facing, and the old note had it 180 out. It is 0 north,
  1 east, 2 south, 3 west - which means the Rimmington portal, at angle 3,
  has been facing west into the bank with its back to the road all along.
- A footprint spread of 4 was one town's answer, not a law. Taverley's
  approved placement spans 32 and looks fine, because the model carries a
  rock base that sits on a slope convincingly. Group 21 now records the
  spread each town was judged at and checks it has not moved, which still
  catches a placement drifting onto ground nobody looked at.

terrain377 also turns out to be uneven: it tracks Rimmington, the square it
was written against, four times better than noise, and Yanille barely at all.
Eight of Yanille's ten portal tiles have no explicit h. The check now prints
every ratio and keeps its hard assertion on Rimmington.

rs2check 0 ERROR / 0 CHECK; poh_battery ALL PASS (54 groups);
poh_mutate 93/93 caught.

